% Text fields with \% and \\, and a tempo change in the body.  \% is a
% percent sign, not the start of a comment, and \\ is a backslash (abc 2.2
% sections 2.2.5 and 8.2).  The parser ended a field at \%, so that
% abc2midi named the track "50\" and yaps printed this title.  A title
% that ends with a backslash made yaps read past its end, and yaps did
% not free the tempo of a Q: field in the body.
X:1
T:50\% faster % a comment
T:C:\\ % after \\, the % starts a comment
T:Ends with a backslash \
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
C D E F |[Q:1/4=180] G A B c |]
